// A read of a `u64:maior` field. It must NOT compile to a program today.
//
// The lowering hands `load` only the field's offset and writes `nativus`
// into the IR (lower/cfg.inc's lwr_load), so before the guard in
// lower/expr.inc's __lwr_field_off this compiled, and emitted
//
//     mov  rax, qword [rax+0]
//
// -- a little-endian read of a big-endian place, with nothing downstream able
// to tell. The guard makes the lowering refuse (an `rassert`: exsc dies with
// SIGILL, shell status 132) instead. That is a trap rather than a diagnostic
// on purpose: the source is correct and no spec 13 code describes it; what is
// missing is in the compiler, and docs/asm-conventions.md 1.3 routes "an
// internal contract violation -- a compiler bug" to `rassert`, never to an
// `EXS-E` code.
//
// Milestone M6 of the wire-codec plan carries the order into `load`/`store`
// and removes the guard. Then this directory changes from `exsc-exit=132` to
// a program that builds a `Par` and returns a byte of it, which is the test
// the guard is standing in for.

@transitus
publica structura Par {
    valor: u64:maior
}

functio lege(p: Par) -> u64:maior {
    redde p.valor;
}

publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    redde 0;
}
